+(defn studio-promote-candidate!
+  "Marker first, candidate second, with an authoritative read barrier after
+   each append. A returned accepted candidate is therefore already classified
+   as Studio-gated at the lowest activation hand.
+
+   R1a · TRAP-2 — the gate is read BEFORE the marker is minted: an already
+   REPORTED gate refuses outright, and a gate whose current marker would not
+   be byte-identical to this call's proposed nil-report marker refuses as a
+   conflict, rather than silently superseding it. Only an absent gate, or one
+   already carrying this exact marker (the true retry case), proceeds."
+  [runtime spec source expected-instances opts]
